[{"id":"VRCE-7-88-1","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":88,"verse":1,"english":"After the great Rșis Vālmīki had said this, Rāma, on beholding the daughter of Janaka resembling a celestial, in the midst of the assembly, with folded hands, said.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.859,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-97-1"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7088001","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"f4b58cf012c4028928ade57401aeaf5dca6a1b7157d0fb03ce4801392822dd6d","compact":"6f18f8eaa4a7f57e409c24f51d86b62013c6fdf1b2062f3362058d37aa3e7f3b","nasal":"35921879e8a68f4d060b68161b17e7da29d702d3abc3c30df18f924143b21a20"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-88-2","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":88,"verse":2,"english":"O great one, you are conversant with piety. By your words shorn of sin, I have been convinced that Janaki is of pure ways. Still, O Brāhmaṇa, what you have commanded shall be carried out; let Sītā produce testimony of the purity of her character.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.69,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-97-2"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7088002","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"d49adb254609d29b7dda55f14eb5aa3ff64dd1520c8420ad1222eb1d00f3646b","compact":"dc6fb21bcd447b251b970aa56440fd23c6644b5dfa178441a418283e91982c41","nasal":"dc6fb21bcd447b251b970aa56440fd23c6644b5dfa178441a418283e91982c41"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-88-3","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":88,"verse":3,"english":"O Brāhmaṇa, vilification of the people is very powerful. Although I know that Jānaki has not been touched by any sin still I have renounced her. Do you therefore forgive me.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.569,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-97-4"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7088003","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"174fb51949e8af33972d5a150f6b974ddbf4bf3f741cba909322690b2bc8ec6d","compact":"e9d40c88497c62880d205c6da358f63dac4196b8a1796a824e5e7a7ce1bc1eb5","nasal":"99773c8372cb35052b4aca6339d49b3d89d8c7b388871cfceaf2f3c084caefa0"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-88-4","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":88,"verse":4,"english":"I know that these twin brothers Kusa and Lava are my sons. Yet if Janaki gives evidence of her own purity before the assembly I shall be greatly satisfied.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-97-5"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7088004","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"1575e9bc195961c5e28c803a0d65a27575ea9cfc26aefc0bbe4817141003f65b","compact":"d5c5f569fe02f309e294f57790f1ad4cfc577e3fa6e53b0b43e48c8665a5ce30","nasal":"d5c5f569fe02f309e294f57790f1ad4cfc577e3fa6e53b0b43e48c8665a5ce30"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-88-5","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":88,"verse":5,"english":"Being apprised of Rama's intention as to Sītā's trial the celestials all came there on the occasion. The Adityas, Vasus, Rudras, Visvadeva, Maruts, Sadhyas, Siddhas, Nagas, and Rsis placing Brahmā before them, all came there.","alignment":{"type":"split","confidence":0.579,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-97-6","DUTT-7-97-7"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7088005","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"c7dcafc44ce32bb78c5e0039e396e528bb41be2f4fba7cb09ac1f41433c619fd","compact":"b10aaa86d8cb0cde6f51be8c78989b8d6ae347b26c95e6f0fd47716da82c3026","nasal":"b10aaa86d8cb0cde6f51be8c78989b8d6ae347b26c95e6f0fd47716da82c3026"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-88-6","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":88,"verse":6,"english":"The Adityas, Vasus, Rudras, Visvadeva, Maruts, Sadhyas, Siddhas, Nagas, and Rsis placing Brahmā before them, all came there.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.57,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-97-7"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7088006","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"f09ae2938290c1c9563de36ed0caa75dd7f3edb59267182f20b02de516da5390","compact":"b9f54ead60bae49ca25bb8e99ff3963070d22a3e1f006fe09f4cdbff9dab25d1","nasal":"844ed8dd9636f67561e9e621fd5bbc9d040ce1947af17a3ca7e2aedf479f74b9"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-88-7","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":88,"verse":7,"english":"As soon as those words were uttered, sweet, fragrant, cold air, the witness of virtue and vice, blowing mildly, excited the joy of the assembly. People, hailing from various countries, with all attention began to witness this wondrous and unthought of event. In the golden age only the celestial wind used to blow, and it now blew even in the Tretā Yuga and forsooth it was a matter of exceeding surprise.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.869,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-97-9"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7088007","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"b537554e486e9608d37dba836211df47877aef95993c8263b2cd086322b85bd8","compact":"9babae790508316e328ec5457cebe5f1c688ec98807ee4bbdbde64f28c19bf9f","nasal":"9401e95e25ba73168695ed2576053eac5b15e213fcc6fa42fc3c9dde8977ac9d"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-88-8","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":88,"verse":8,"english":"As soon as those words were uttered, sweet, fragrant, cold air, the witness of virtue and vice, blowing mildly, excited the joy of the assembly. People, hailing from various countries, with all attention began to witness this wondrous and unthought of event. In the golden age only the celestial wind used to blow, and it now blew even in the Tretā Yuga and forsooth it was a matter of exceeding surprise.","alignment":{"ty